# It shows text in a corner, and that is all it may do -- no network, no audio,
# no devices.
#
# `filesystem` is here for ONE reason and it is worth stating, because leaving
# it out is the more obvious-looking choice and it is wrong: every EmUI program
# reads /system/fonts/font.ttf at startup. Without this capability notifyd came
# up, drew its banner frames, and rendered NOT ONE CHARACTER -- empty rounded
# boxes in the corner, because the font open failed and there were no glyphs to
# draw. The capability system worked exactly as designed; the declaration was
# simply wrong.
#
# Narrowing this to a read-only /system/fonts binding in notifyd.ns is the
# proper fix and is left as one.

filesystem     # the font, and nothing else it actually opens
gpu            # a window is a GPU resource
